\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Danish bonds rally as  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  stoke rate cut talk\b0\par\par\uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2022\par 15:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates with analyst comment, context)\par \par \uc2 By Dhara Ranasinghe\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Denmark's short-dated borrowing costs fell on Wednesday, as news of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Danish crown stoked speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would soon resort to an interest rate cut.\par \par \uc2 According to data released on Tuesday, \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month sold 47 billion Danish crowns, worth more than $7 billion, to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg against the euro.\par \par \uc2 While it has been selling crowns to stabilise its strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March 2021, December marked the biggest monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early 2020.\par \par \uc2 Those purchases have taken \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to the highest since 2015, at almost 530 billion Danish crowns ($81 bln).\par \par \uc2 But economists reckon authorities may have to follow up those \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by cutting interest rates.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have regular monetary policy meetings but the board of governors convenes whenever necessary. It usually announces rate decisions on a Thursday at 5pm local time.\par \par \uc2 Another cut soon would follow a September move, which came after months of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to sufficiently weaken the crown.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sole mandate is to maintain the peg and keep the crown within a band of 7.29252 to 7.62824 crowns per euro.\par \par \uc2 The rate cut speculation, is now playing out in bond markets where yields fell sharply, suggesting investors are starting to position for such a move.\par \par \uc2 The yield on Denmark's three-year bond was down almost 7 basis points (bps) on Wednesday at -0.50%.\par \par \uc2 Five-year bond yields were down 3 bps at -0.34%.\par \par \uc2 "They have shown a long-standing willingness to defend the exchange rate peg and that won't change anytime soon," said David Oxley, a senior European economist at Capital Economics, referring to \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy makers.\par \par \uc2 "In September, the rate cut was a logical solution to the upward pressure on the peg so if the crown is under pressure again that they will do what it takes to maintain the peg."\par \par \uc2 While money market futures so far suggest only a 20% chance of a 10 bps rate cut in February, speculation is building.\par \par \uc2 Nordea\uc2  analysts said another rate cut could be imminent while Soren Kristensen, chief economist at \uc2 Sydbank\uc2 , saw a possible 10-15 bps move during the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 Oxley at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said Denmark could cut rates to as low as -0.75% without opening up too much of a gap with the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key rate at -0.50%.\par \par \uc2 At -0.60%, the key Danish interest rate is already among the lowest in the world and a rate cut would contrast with policy in most other developed economies, where central banks are scaling back stimulus and lifting borrowing costs from ultra-low levels as inflation picks up.\par \par \uc2 Not all see a rate cut as a done deal. \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  noted upward crown pressure was now receding, meaning \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be considered sufficient.\par \par \uc2 Claus Hvidegaard, head of fixed income research \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at SEB, says higher \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were more of a reflection of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's wish to boost excess liquidity, and keep money market rates stable versus the euro area.\par \par \uc2 "We see it as much more of a liquidity exercise, so we think they will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to boost liquidity before they consider another rate cut."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Dhara Ranasinghe in London and Nikolaj Skydsgaard in Copenhagen; Editing by Sujata Rao, Mark Potter and Hugh Lawson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-1-5T15:59:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220105ei1502cq1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
