\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Danish  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves shrink after large  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2020\par 17:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comments, background)\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Jan 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by more than 4 billion crowns in December after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made its largest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in three months, it said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We need to go back four years, since there has been an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  three months in a row, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is potentially not done," chief economist at \uc2 Arbejdernes Landsbank\uc2 , Jeppe Borre, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to 435.4 billion crowns ($65.05 billion) in December from 440.7 billion crowns at the end of November, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It bought 4.1 billion crowns in December to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable against the euro, to which it is pegged, it said.\par \par \uc2 In October and November, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only bought 0.4 and 1.2 billion crowns respectively.\par \par \uc2 Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key rate to its lowest level ever in September, mirroring a cut by the \uc2 ECB\uc2 , the crown has steadily weakened to levels not seen since 2015.\par \par \uc2 In 2015, the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to stave off foreign investors buying crowns in the hopes that Denmark would abandon its fixed peg to the euro.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate cut has, all things being equal, been more significant than that of the \uc2 ECB\uc2 , which contributes to the weakening of the crown," chief economist at \uc2 Arbejdernes Landsbank\uc2 , Jeppe Borre, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 6.6934 Danish crowns) (Reporting by Nikolaj Skydsgaard; Editing by Kirsten Donovan and Nick Macfie) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-1-3T17:40:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200103eg1302a0t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
