\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Denmark Central Bank Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  Is Possible -- 1Q  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 By Charles Duxbury \par \uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2017\par 00:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  looks unlikely to move interest rates in the first quarter, but it could return to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets if the Danish krone's exchange rate begins to veer off target.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Denmark's Nationalbank aims to make life easier for exporters to the important eurozone market, as well as keep inflation low and steady, by tightly controlling the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It's only policy aim is to keep the euro's exchange rate within 2.25% of 7.46038 kroner.\par \par \uc2 The krone has been on the strong side over recent weeks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have taken note. Analysts expect the bank to react soon and begin selling kroner.\par \par \uc2 "We do not believe that the bank will allow a further appreciation of the krone," said Jan Storup Nielsen at \uc2 Nordea Bank\uc2  in Copenhagen.\par \par \uc2 Of vital importance for Danish interest rates throughout 2017 will be the actions of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Further easing in Frankfurt could send the euro lower against the krone and force Danish policy makers into counter measures.\par \par \uc2 However, as the \uc2 ECB\uc2  looks likely to leave its policy levers largely unchanged in the short term, Nationalbank may do likewise.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Storup Nielsen expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key interest rate to remain at minus 0.65% into 2018. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Main Policy Rate  Last-Quarter Rate  Current Rate   Outlook \par Deposit Rate       -0.65% Oct. 4     -0.65% Jan. 3   Hold \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Charles Duxbury at charles.duxbury@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 03, 2017 18:26 ET (23:26 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170103ed13003s9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
