\par\par \b \uc2 NORDIC MORNING BRIEFING: Earnings and Central Banks in Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dominic Chopping \par \uc2 1,602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2016\par 04:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par  \par Nordic Macro \par 0600 Finland October Consumer \par      Confidence \par 0600 Norway August Unemployment \par 0700 Sweden October CCI \par 0730 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sweden Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Rate Call \par 0800 Norway Norges Bank Rate Call \par  \par Other Macro \par 0800 EuroZone September M3 \par      Money Supply \par 0830 UK 3Q GDP \par 1230 US September Durable \par      Goods Orders \par 1230 US Initial Jobless Claims \par 1400 US September Pending Home \par      Sales \par  \par Nordic Equities \par Autoliv 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 DNB ASA\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par Nokia Corp 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Statoil ASA\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Svenska Cellulosa AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par  \par Other Equities \par ABB Ltd 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alphabet Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon.com Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par BASF SE 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Blackstone Group LP\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par Bristolmyers Squibb Co 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 BT Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  2Q \par Colgate-Palmolive Co 3Q \par ConocoPhillips 3Q \par Deutsche Bank 3Q \par Dow Chemical Co 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dr Pepper Snapple Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 EQT Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Expedia Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par Ford Motor Co 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kia Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Linkedin Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nomura Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  2Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stanley Black & Decker Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par STMicroelectronics NV 3Q \par Telefonica SA 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Parcel Service Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 ZTE Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A hectic day Thursday sees regional heavyweights \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Statoil\f28 \uc2 \f2  kick things off on the earnings front before two keenly eyed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy meetings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sweden's Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is the first to announce the result of its latest monetary policy meeting and although no change is expected to rates, the rate path or the asset-purchase program, September's disappointing inflation reading could pose questions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "After most things went the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's way so far this year, the reading on inflation in September suddenly stirred things up a bit," Handelsbanken said. However, it expects the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to adopt a wait-and-see stance, with both October and November inflation readings due before the Dec. 20 policy meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If the majority of factors for the unexpected price trends in October prove to be only temporary, and if the inflation rate rises again, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's stance should be more or less unchanged, we think. On the other hand, further disinflationary shocks should likely push for policy easing once again, most likely involving first-hand expanded asset purchases," it said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is also expected to stand pat, after it indicated in September that a rate change in the near term was unlikely.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "On the one hand, NOK has been stronger, inflation lower and money market spreads higher than expected," noted \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "On the other hand oil price and rates abroad are higher. The summing up will probably indicate that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  has not changed its view significantly. It should be neutral to the market." \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \par EUR/NOK \par 0250 GMT 9.0192-242 \par Previous 9.0254-304 \par %Chg -0.07 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par 0250 GMT 9.7144-244 \par Previous 9.7133-233 \par %Chg +0.01 \par  \par USD/NOK \par 0250 GMT 8.2785-845 \par Previous 8.2728-88 \par %Chg +0.07 \par  \par USD/SEK \par 0250 GMT 8.9175-265 \par Previous 8.9045-135 \par %Chg +0.15 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EUR/DKK continues to trade with a heavy tone below 7.4400, with the DKK supported by the world's second-largest current account surplus and safe-haven demand for DKK on the back of high political uncertainty in Europe, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We forecast EUR/DKK at 7.4425 in 12 months and thus for the pair to continue to trade at the low end of the historical trading range," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It noted that EUR/DKK three-month \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forward outright is trading around 7.4370, above the 7.4350 level where \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske\f28 \uc2 \f2  would expect \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Denmark\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the lower bound for EUR/DKK. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40 1435.41  -0.07% \par OMXS30 1454.21  +0.23% \par OBX     564.64  -2.14% \par OMXC20 1025.75  -1.04% \par OMXH25 3517.73  +0.18% \par  \par Brent crude: $49.98 \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic stock markets had a largely negative session Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European indexes traded lower as company results, weaker crude oil prices and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments dampened enthusiasm, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Saxo Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Both anticipation for, and arrival of, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  production cut deal have boosted crude prices for several weeks now, but now that the ink had dried it appears investors have their doubts about the agreement's real impact on global supplies," Saxo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "These doubts have now pushed WTI prices back below the $50/barrel benchmark, impacting risk sentiment."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beyond oil, the main risk event remains the US presidential election, Saxo added. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices were little changed in Asia following declines in the U.S. that came as the market focused on \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's lack of real progress in convincing members to join a production cut deal rather than a surprise drop in U.S. crude inventories.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A closer look at the U.S. data actually shows the latest 553,000-barrel decline in stocks was centered on the West Coast, which is isolated from the rest of the network, said ANZ Research.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Inventories actually increased along East and Gulf Coasts," the bank adds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0242 GMT, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nymex\f28 \uc2 \f2  was down 1 cent at $49.17 a barrel, while Brent was unchanged at $49.98 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's competition watchdog on Wednesday announced they will attempt to settle a longstanding antitrust case and that the state-controlled energy company would soon submit concrete commitments to change behaviors in exchange for escaping a hefty fine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are now putting the final touch to our commitment proposal. It will be sent to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  shortly," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alexander Medvedev\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Gazprom's deputy chairman, said following a meeting with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 's competition commissioner, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Margrethe Vestager\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Two people familiar with the negotiations said that nailing down the outstanding details for a preliminary settlement agreement might still take "a couple of weeks."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In essence, we have a deal," one of those people said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ericsson AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  appointed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Borje Ekholm\f28 \uc2 \f2  as chief executive Wednesday, as the struggling telecom-equipment provider looks to turn around its business amid waning demand and stiff global competition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Ekholm has been an \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ericsson\f28 \uc2 \f2  board member for the past 10 years. He joins \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ericsson\f28 \uc2 \f2 's executive team from his position as CEO of Patricia Industries, a division within \f28 \uc2 \f2 Investor AB\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a Swedish investment company that is \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ericsson\f28 \uc2 \f2 's largest shareholder, controlling over 20% of its voting rights.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The news sent \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ericsson\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares as much as 3% higher in morning trading in Stockholm.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ericsson\f28 \uc2 \f2  had been looking for a new CEO since it ousted \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hans Vestberg\f28 \uc2 \f2  in July, as the company battles slowing demand for its cellphone towers and switches and faces competition from China's Huawei Technologies Co. and Nordic rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking at a news conference in Stockholm, Mr. Ekholm said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ericsson\f28 \uc2 \f2  must continue to trim expenses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are clearly challenged right now--we have to make adjustments to our cost structure," he said. "That's something that has to go on."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Ekholm said he aimed to make \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ericsson\f28 \uc2 \f2  profitable again by prioritizing parts of its business while divesting others. He didn't provide more details.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We have to establish profitability first," he said, adding he then wanted to "focus on building a strong company for the long term--five years-plus."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NORWAY: Telenor SA (TEL.OS) Wednesday posted a third-quarter net loss due to costs related to the part sale of its stake in Amsterdam-based peer \f28 \uc2 \f2 VimpelCom Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .(VIP).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Norwegian telecom provider's net loss for the period ending Sept. 30 was 4.82 billion Norwegian kroner ($540 million), compared with a net loss of NOK1.77 billion a year earlier, while third-quarter revenue was NOK32.79 billion, up slightly from NOK31.84 billion in the same period last year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telenor\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which is majority-owned by the Norwegian state, attributed the net loss mainly to its 33% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 VimpelCom\f28 \uc2 \f2 , nearly one-fourth of which it started selling through a public offering last month. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telenor\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the adjusted price of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 VimpelCom\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares resulted in a total impairment loss of NOK2.4 billion, as well as a loss of NOK3.2 billion related to a reclassification of translation differences previously recognized in other comprehensive income.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NORWAY: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea Bank AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NDA.SK) Wednesday posted a 14% rise in third-quarter net profit as income from its wholesale banking activities helped offset sluggish net interest income. Net profit at the Stockholm-based bank climbed to 888 million euros ($966.0 million) in the three months ending Sept. 30 from EUR780 million in the same period a year earlier, beating expectations of EUR818 million, according to a FactSet poll.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The third quarter was characterised by a stable environment with low volatility on the financial markets but also continued low growth," Chief Executive Casper von Koskull said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Total revenues held up well in the quarter...we continue to believe the trough levels are over. Negative rates have put pressure on deposit margins, which was partly offset by higher lending margins."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dong Energy A/S\f28 \uc2 \f2  (DENERG.KO) said Wednesday it had started a review of options for its oil and gas business, a unit it previously said wasn't central to its long-term strategy. The Danish utility and wind-farm developer said in a statement that \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  was conducting a preliminary market assessment but no decision had been taken on whether to divest.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Dominic Chopping at dominic.chopping@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @domchopping @WSJNordics\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 26, 2016 22:54 ET (02:54 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161027ecar000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
