\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Denmark \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Could  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Market -- 4Q  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 By Charles Duxbury \par \uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2016\par 23:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Denmark\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has shown no sign that it is preparing to change interest rates, and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market looks likely to continue as the policy tool of choice over the coming months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have its eye on a recent weakening of the Danish krone and will act to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the drop extends into the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's only policy aim is to keep the euro's exchange rate within 2.25% of 7.46038 kroner to control inflation and provide stability for domestic businesses that look to the eurozone as an important export market. It has no target for the inflation rate.\par \par \uc2 Further ahead, analysts are flagging that potential political strife in the U.K. or the eurozone could lift the krone without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  help as investors sell euros or pounds for the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  identified the Italian constitutional referendum on Dec. 4 and talks on the U.K.'s withdrawal from the \uc2 European Union\uc2  as clouds on the horizon.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell kroner if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks like it is rising as high as it did straight after the Brexit vote.\par \par \uc2 On interest rates, the current level looks set to persist. \uc2 Nordea\uc2  analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy rate to be maintained at -0.65% until the end of 2017. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Main Policy Rate  Last-Quarter Rate  Current Rate   Outlook \par Deposit Rate       -0.65% July 7    -0.65% Oct. 4    Hold \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Charles Duxbury at charles.duxbury@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 04, 2016 17:42 ET (21:42 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161004eca4003sz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
