\par\par \b \uc2 NORDIC MORNING BRIEFING: Nordic Manufacturing PMIs in Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dominic Chopping   \par \uc2 1,489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2016\par 05:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par  \par Nordic Macro \par 0630 Sweden June PMI \par      Manufacturing \par 0700 Norway June PMI \par      Manufacturing \par 0800 Norway June Registered \par      Unemployment \par 0900 Denmark June PMI \par      Manufacturing \par  \par Other Macro \par 0830 UK June PMI Manufacturing \par 0900 Euro Zone May Unemployment \par 1400 US June ISM Manufacturing \par  \par GLOBAL NEWS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 S&P cut the investment-grade credit ratings of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  by a notch, saying the U.K.'s vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  reduces its budget flexibility and reflects a loss of political solidarity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 S&P now has the \uc2 EU\uc2  at double-A, the third-highest investment-grade ratings. The credit ratings firm said the outlook is stable, reflecting S&P's view that under most scenarios, including any U.K. withdrawal from future budget commitments, its current rating on the \uc2 EU\uc2  will stay at the current level. The ratings agency affirmed its double-A-plus credit ratings on the U.S., pointing to the country's economic resiliency, bolstered by its status as the issuer of the world's leading reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 China's official manufacturing purchasing managers' index, a gauge of the nation's factory activity, edged down in June, ending three straight months of expansion, official data showed Friday.\par \par \uc2 The index fell to 50.0--the mark that separates expansion from contraction--from 50.1 a month ago, suggesting the world's second-largest economy is still struggling to gain momentum. The June PMI matched a median forecast of 50.0 by 13 economists polled by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 China's official nonmanufacturing purchasing managers' index, a gauge of activity outside factory floors, rose to 53.7 in June from 53.1 in May.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's latest tankan survey showed that manufacturers' sentiment remained solid in the second quarter, although the poll doesn't fully take into account the impact on business confidence of the Brexit vote.\par \par \uc2 The main index of the quarterly survey released Friday showed that sentiment among big manufacturers remained unchanged at plus 6 in the April-June quarter. The reading compares with a median forecast for plus 4 by 17 economists polled by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Turkey opened a new area of membership talks with the \uc2 European Union\uc2  on Thursday, but bloc officials made clear there was no prospect of further advancement to Ankara's bid in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Turkey had pressed for an advancement of its talks on membership as a condition of the deal to take back migrants who cross into Greece and the \uc2 EU\uc2 . The \uc2 EU\uc2  fulfilled that pledge by opening what is called a chapter in the accession discussions.\par \par \uc2 There are 35 chapters in the accession talks. The \uc2 EU\uc2  has begun discussion on 16 of them, including the chapter on financial and budgetary provisions which were opened Thursday. But talks on only one chapter have been completed and the \uc2 EU\uc2  hasn't opened discussion on any of the most sensitive topics.\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis President \uc2 James Bullard\uc2  said Thursday the U.S. economy was in an era of modest growth that would keep unemployment and inflation at their current levels for the next 2 1/2 years.\par \par \uc2 "Key macroeconomic variables including real output growth, the unemployment rate, and inflation appear to be at or near values that are likely to persist over the forecast horizon," Mr. Bullard said. "Any further cyclical adjustment is likely to be relatively minor."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Bullard also said the U.K.'s decision to exit the \uc2 European Union\uc2  is unlikely to seriously disrupt the U.S. or global economies.\par \par \uc2 "I think what we've learned in the past five days is that it was a shock but global markets held up fairly well," Mr. Bullard said. "Global markets were able to absorb the shock, reprice, and look forward to the future."\par \par \uc2 The U.S. asked Moscow to force the regime of President Bashar al-Assad to ground its air force as part of a proposal that could lead to greater cooperation with Russia in Syria, according to officials familiar with the offer.\par \par \uc2 If the Russians get the regime to ground its air force, the Pentagon then would consider helping Moscow with its targeting in Syria, to ensure its strikes hit the \uc2 Nusra Front\uc2  and Islamic State militant groups, rather than the U.S.-backed moderate opposition, the officials said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It's a busy day of PMI data in the region Friday and SEB said that June's manufacturing PMIs increased markedly in the eurozone, especially Germany, defying expectations of marginally lower readings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Hence, outside of the U.K., Brexit fears do not seem to have affected sentiment in manufacturing much."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Norway, June registered unemployment is due and will be especially interesting after seasonally adjusted registered unemployment increased by nearly 1,000 in May, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "That was in line with our view that the economy is still too weak to avoid a further increase in unemployment."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It expects a further increase in unemployment in June, but at a somewhat slower pace. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \par EUR/NOK \par 0150 GMT 9.2808-58 \par Previous 9.2887-937 \par %Chg -0.09 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par 0150 GMT 9.3857-957 \par Previous 9.3897-997 \par %Chg -0.04 \par  \par USD/NOK \par 0150 GMT 8.3545-605 \par Previous 8.3604-64 \par %Chg -0.07 \par  \par USD/SEK \par 0150 GMT 8.4494-584 \par Previous 8.4553-643 \par %Chg -0.07 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There may be extra nervousness and fluctuations in the Danish krone in the coming weeks and months as a result of the low visibility with respect to Britain's position in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the resulting major economic uncertainty, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It said that price activity in EUR/DKK and excess liquidity in the banking sector indicates that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Denmark\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets both before and after the U.K.'s vote last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But there is no sign that the National Bank has been forced to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  massively by the British Brexit," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2  said, noting that indications point to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  totaling around DKK5 billion ($0.745 billion) on June 24, which, it said, is not dramatic. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40 1414.09 +1.28% \par OMXS30 1323.57 +1.07% \par OBX     541.23 +2.64% \par OMXC20 1007.96 +1.27% \par OMXH25 3198.2  +1.39% \par  \par Brent crude: $50.07 \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic markets had a generally positive session Thursday, though gains were modest as markets began to settle after a volatile week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "European markets took a breath first thing and opened lower, with oil also showing weakness," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Saxo Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Equities then reversed from their lows to turn positive," Saxo added, but noted "it's probably time for a pause" in the dramatic recovery uptick. A two-day surge in the price of oil--on the back of a bigger-than-expected inventory decline and a continued production slowdown--ran out of steam Thursday, with WTI falling back below $50 a barrel, while Brent crude headed lower after touching $51. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices rebounded in Asia following sharp losses in the U.S. session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Around 0330 GMT, Brent crude was trading at $50.07, up 36 cents while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nymex\f28 \uc2 \f2  was at $48.63, a gain of 31 cents. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: Denmark's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vestas Wind Systems A/S\f28 \uc2 \f2  (VWS.KO) said Thursday it has received an order for 22 turbines to be installed at the Lyrestad wind park in Mariestad, Sweden, with power produced from the development sold to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  as part of the tech company's drive to power its entire \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on clean energy. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  said at the end of last year that it was purchasing a further 842 megawatts of renewable energy and, in addition to Thursday's deal with the Swedish wind farm, it has signed a similar agreement with a new 50-turbine project near Stavanger in Norway. In total, the two new wind farms will provide 236 megawatts of energy and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  has signed long-term contracts to purchase all energy produced from both projects, it said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAS AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  (SAS.SK) said Thursday it has sold its remaining 20% stake in Nordic regional airline Wideroe, completing a plan it made in 2013 when it was in the midst of extensive restructuring and a debt-reduction exercise as it grappled with high fuel costs and rising competition from discount carriers. The airline, partly owned by the Swedish, Norwegian and Danish governments, sold 80% of Wideroe in September 2013 to WF Holding AS, an investment firm controlled by transport company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Torghatten ASA\f28 \uc2 \f2  for 2 billion Swedish kronor ($237 million). It said at the time that the remaining shares would be divested during 2016.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Dominic Chopping at dominic.chopping@wsj.com; Twitter: @domchopping @WSJNordics\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 30, 2016 23:35 ET (03:35 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160701ec7100084\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
