\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Danish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says upward pressure on crown more likely than downward\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2015\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background, context.)\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Speculation against the Danish crown has usually resulted in a downward pressure, but upward pressure is more likely in the future, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said.\par \par \uc2 "Denmark's role as a creditor nation, where the balance is in our favour, means that future crown crises are likely more often to result in upward pressure," Governor \uc2 Lars Rohde\uc2  said in a speech on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Speculators poured money into Danish assets at the start of the year, betting that Denmark would drop its three-decade-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the euro, following a move by the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to scrap its cap on the franc against the euro.\par \par \uc2 That pressure led \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and suspend government debt issuance in a bid to relieve demand for the crown.\par \par \uc2 Capital flows in January and February were greater than they were earlier, which reflects a trend with the crown, Rohde said. Changes in interest rates have more effect when the crown is weakening, he said, while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have more impact when money is flowing in, Rohde said.\par \par \uc2 Denmark's benchmark certificate of deposit rate has been at -0.75 percent, compared with \uc2 the ECB\uc2 's deposit rate of -0.2 percent, since February. It was cut four times in less than two months when the crown was being forced up.\par \par \uc2 Rohde said on Sept. 16 that the money markets appear to be pricing in an interest rate increase, but he declined to say when and by how much the bank will lift its main rate.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by \uc2 Ole Mikkelsen\uc2 , editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-10-1T10:54:10.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151001eba100agp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
