\par\par \b \uc2 GRAPHIC-Dollar on track for best quarter since Q3 2008, euro the worst\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anirban Nag and Christian Inton   \par \uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 31 (Reuters) - The dollar is on track for its best quarterly performance since 2008 while the euro is set for its worst ever three months, reflecting a divergence in monetary policies between the United States and the euro zone.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/2015/03/30/1409021beb.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/2015/03/30/1409021beb.htm }}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unleashed a 1 trillion euro bond buying programme in March to boost inflation in the euro zone while the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is expected to start tightening policy later this year. Those interest rate differentials work in favour of U.S. Treasuries and have boosted the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index is up 9 percent in the first three months of 2015, its best quarterly performance since July to September 2008, while the euro is down 11 percent during the same period -- the worst quarterly show in its history.\par \par \uc2 "First-quarter expectations were focused on cyclical divergence between the U.S. and rest of the world, and especially Europe," said Steve Englander, global head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Citi. He added that investors were growing impatient with the divergence theme, but had not yet found a replacement for the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the ECB's quantitative easing programme triggered talk of a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Central banks from Switzerland to Sweden moved to prevent their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising sharply against the euro, with the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  shocking markets in Jannuary by abandoning its three-year-old cap on the franc against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The franc soared 40 percent, the biggest one-day move in a major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the era of floating exchange rates, on the day the SNB dropped the cap, before weakening in subsequent weeks. It remains on track for its best quarterly performance in three decades, according to Reuters charts.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to drive down the Danish crown, which hit its highest since 2004. Denmark imposed negative interest rates of -0.75 percent, on a par with the Swiss, and spent billions of dollars to weaken the crown.\par \par \uc2 Those actions saw the crown post its worst quarterly performance in more than 15 years.\par \par \uc2 Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also adopted quantitative easing -- albeit on a smaller scale than the ECB. Despite that, the Swedish crown was on track for its best quarterly performance in two years.. (Reporting by Anirban Nag, graphic by Christian Inton; Editing by Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-31T12:00:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150331eb3v00947\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
