\par\par \b \uc2 Danish Central Banker Pledges to Defend  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Peg--Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Hannon   \par \uc2 702 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 16:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to defending the krone's peg to the euro, and further cuts in its benchmark interest rate, as well as \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, remain options, Governor \uc2 Lars Rohde\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The krone's peg to the euro came under strain after the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a large-scale bond-buying program in January, sending the shared \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spiraling downward. The long-held exchange-rate policy also came into focus because of Switzerland's surprise decision in mid-January to abandon its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cap, catching many investors off guard.\par \par \uc2 In defense of the peg, which has been in place since 1982, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its deposit rate four times in the space of three weeks, with the final move coming at the beginning of February. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth 106.3 billion Danish kroner ($15.39 billion) in January. It bought a further 168.7 billion Danish kroner in February\par \par \uc2 Speaking in London, Mr. Rohde said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the final weeks of February, and pledged to defend the peg, which he said had served the Danish economy well since its introduction.\par \par \uc2 "We are able and we are willing to do whatever it takes to defend the peg," he said. "The peg is the cornerstone of economic policy in Denmark and has very broad based support."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seeks to hold the euro's exchange rate within 2.25% either above or below 7.46038 kroner to keep inflation low and provide stability for exporters.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last reduction in the rate it pays to depositors brought it to minus 0.75%, which Mr. Rohde said was the lowest in the world. But he indicated further cuts were possible.\par \par \uc2 "We have not seen any hoarding of cash," he said. "There is some lower bound for negative interest rates, but we haven't found it yet."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Rohde also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could resume sales of kroner for euros if the peg were to come under pressure again.\par \par \uc2 "There's no upper limit on purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "We have all the instruments to handle the situation. We are able and we are willing to do it."\par \par \uc2 In addition to rate cuts and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in late January \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the novel step of suspending the issuance of government bonds, seeking to deter foreign investment in Danish assets that would strengthen the krone.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Rohde said that policy was equivalent to quantitative easing, the policy embarked on Monday by the ECB, in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys government bonds with newly created money.\par \par \uc2 "The Danish government has almost two years of free financing requirements as a deposit with the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "This works like a QE \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If a government is paying back on old bond issues, they finance it by drawing money from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But that is almost the same as issuing bonds that are bought by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 He added that if bond sales were to be suspended throughout 2015, the amount of quantitative easing involved would be roughly equivalent to that carried out by the ECB.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Rohde said the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's Jan. 15 decision to abandon its cap on the Swiss franc's exchange rate against the euro had been a "genuine surprise," and prompted foreign investors to speculate that Denmark might be forced to take similar action as the euro continued to weaken.\par \par \uc2 But Mr. Rohde stressed that "we are not Switzerland," noting big differences in the degree of popular support for and long-term commitment to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the two countries.\par \par \uc2 "The Swiss (arrangement) was not a peg, it was a ceiling," he said. "It was declared to be temporary. And it was not part of an understanding by all parties that this was the way we should go on."\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Hannon at paul.hannon@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 12, 2015 11:22 ET (15:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150312eb3c002kk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
