\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-\uc2 Danish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  has resources to keep crown stable: governor\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2015\par 15:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds more quotes, analyst comment, context)\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Ole Mikkelsen\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Feb 6 (Reuters) - \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has other means of holding the crown steady against the euro which it has not yet used, Governor \uc2 Lars Rohde\uc2  told Reuters on Friday, adding it will do "whatever it takes" to protect its fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 He said negative interest rates will stay in place for "quite a long time" and could be lowered further. But he would not be drawn into details of future actions.\par \par \uc2 The normally reclusive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief has launched a media offensive in the past two days, emphasising \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decades-old commitment to the peg; rare verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which some analysts took to be a sign of its concern.\par \par \uc2 The bank spent over 100 billion Danish crowns ($15 billion) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a tight range against a weakening euro and has cut its deposit rate four times in three weeks to an unprecedented low of -0.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 "We have unlimited amounts of crowns available. We can let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grow indefinitely. It is an option that we can use and it is unlimited. We are ready to do whatever it takes," he told Reuters by telephone, echoing a phrase that \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  used to calm market alarm about the euro.\par \par \uc2 "There are other tools in the toolbox, than those you have seen," he said.\par \par \uc2 Responsibility for Denmark's monetary policy is unusually concentrated in the governor, a position which Rohde took in 2013. There is no rate-setting committee, nor are there scheduled meetings with minutes for investors to glean for policy clues.\par \par \uc2 Rohde took a substantial pay cut from his previous role as the chief executive of ATP -- the country's largest pension fund which runs the state-mandated pension scheme for all Danes. ATP posted record results in some years of the financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 UNLIMITED RESERVES\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe Rohde was signalling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the preferred 'tool' to steady the crown because of his repetition that there were no limits on foreign reserve growth -- the result of selling crowns to hold down the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he would allow reserves to climb to 100 percent or even 200 percent of gross domestic product (GDP), Rohde said: "I do not fear that".\par \par \uc2 Switzerland built foreign reserves worth 80 percent of GDP before it scrapped its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cap to the euro on Jan. 15, diverting pressure onto the crown.\par \par \uc2 "It may well be that they (Denmark) have more tools as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said, but it is most likely that they will let the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grow," said \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  Senior Analyst Jens Naervig Pedersen.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised markets last week when it suspended government bond issues, in effect taking out demand for 75 billion Danish crowns.\par \par \uc2 "The suspension of issuance of government bonds is a Danish version of QE (quantitative easing). It provides downward pressure on government bond yields and has a spillover effect on mortgage bonds," Rohde said.\par \par \uc2 "That makes it less attractive to hold crowns."\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he would launch a "real" QE scheme, meaning a bond-buying programme like the ECB's, he said: "I would not rule anything out, but we have no plans." ($1 = 6.5050 Danish crowns) (Writing by Sabina Zawadzki; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-9T14:55:16.000Z  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150206eb2600jah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
