\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-More Danish rate cuts seen; next stop -- wider  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  band\b0\par\par\uc2 762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2015\par 07:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats item to additional subscribers with no changes)\par \par \uc2 * Crown seen as safer haven since Swiss scrapped cap\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2  using rate cuts, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb crown\par \par \uc2 * Still has bolder option of widening trading band\par \par \uc2 * Analysts do not see Denmark scrapping its peg\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Ole Mikkelsen\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Jan 30 (Reuters) - Denmark is likely to cut its deposit rate deeper into negative territory and could widen the crown's trading band if bolder action is needed to relieve pressure on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2 Investors have piled into the Danish crown since the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shocked markets on Jan. 15 by scrapping the franc's cap to the euro and cut interest rates to levels that are below Denmark's, making the crown more attractive.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision last week to launch a landmark bond-buying programme with new money to weaken the euro has also bolstered the crown.\par \par \uc2 Rising pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spurred speculation that Denmark may follow the Swiss and scrap its 15-year-old peg to the euro. But, analysts say that is unlikely, pointing to a number of other options the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can resort to before having to consider abandoning the regime.\par \par \uc2 Under the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM2), Denmark agreed to keep the crown at 2.25 percent either side of the parity rate of 7.46038 crowns to the euro. But in practice, the crown has not moved more than 0.5 percent on either side, as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when necessary, has kept it in check.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has several tools they can use before they have to give up the fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and so far they have only used two," said Citi Economist Tina Mortensen.\par \par \uc2 "In addition to lowering interest rates further, they can build up reserves. But they can also reintroduce a three-year lending facility and they can use the fluctuation band more ... Denmark can let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuate 15 percent around the central parity and still meet ERM2 requirements," she said.\par \par \uc2 While Denmark agreed to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  very close to the euro, ERM2 rules allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other participants, ranging from Cyprus and Malta to Slovenia and Lithuania, to fluctuate 15 percent either side of parity as a general rule.\par \par \uc2 A sluggish economic recovery in the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , prospects of deflation in some countries and political uncertainty due to factors such as the election of the far-left Syriza party in Greece are all weighing on the euro.\par \par \uc2 "With many uncertainties still facing the euro area and with Danish monetary policy already loose, the pressure will likely remain ... and a recalibration of the current trading range cannot be ruled out," \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 RESERVES AT RECORD?\par \par \uc2 Before a potential widening of the trading range, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has plenty of room to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cutting interest rates to curb the crown. At the very least it could lower its benchmark rate to -0.75 percent to match the Swiss rate, or below, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key rate to -0.50 percent, the third cut in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Unlike Russia, which is burning up its foreign reserves to defend the ailing rouble, undermining financial stability, \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2  is building its reserves by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb a strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jes Asmussen, chief economist at Handelsbanken Capital Markets, estimates that in January the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record $100 billion ($15 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by selling crowns to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That suggests foreign reserves -- which stood at 447 billion crowns ($68 billion) at the end of December, or a quarter of Danish gross domestic product -- could bypass their record level of 514 billion crowns, held in July 2012. Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data is due on Feb. 3.\par \par \uc2 As the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policies show, there is such a thing as having too much in reserves. The Danish level, however, is far off the 100 percent of GDP that the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  held before it scrapped the franc's cap.\par \par \uc2 "The market is testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment. The question is when the market realises that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will insist on keeping the crown close to the euro," chief economist \uc2 Helge Pedersen\uc2  from Nordea said. ($1 = 6.5837 Danish crowns) (Additional reporting by Anirban Nag in London; Editing by Sabina Zawadzki and Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-5T06:01:00.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150202eb22006hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
