\par\par \b \uc2 Danish crown falls after Denmark's cuts rates again\b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2015\par 16:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 29 (Reuters) - The Danish crown fell to a day's low against the euro on Thursday after \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took interest rates deeper into negative territory to ward off upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered the certificate of deposit rate to a record low of -0.5 percent, from -0.35 percent, and said the rate cut followed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 This was the third rate cut in two weeks, broadly a response to the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to embark on one-trillion-euro worth of additional stimulus for the euro zone economy.\par \par \uc2 In afternoon trade, the crown weakened to 7.4452 crowns per euro from 7.4440 before the rate cut, before recovering to trade at 7.4438.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few days after buying 6.9 billion crowns ($1.1 billion) in the market between September and November 2014.\par \par \uc2 An \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  often precedes a rate cut in \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Anirban Nag; editing by \uc2 Patrick Graham\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-29T16:17:23.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150129eb1t00glc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
