\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX- \highlight22\uc2 Denmark \highlight\uc2  and the ERM II, how  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  works\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2015\par 15:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS, Jan 20 (Reuters) - Financial markets expect the Danish crown might appreciate after an expected \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision on Thursday to start quantitative easing, threatening to break out of its narrow fixed fluctuation band against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Below are some key elements of the Danish crown's fixing in the band, called the Exchange Rate Mechanism II, which is the waiting room for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prove they are stable against the euro before a country joins the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  area.\par \par \uc2 * The Danish crown joined ERM II on January 1, 1999. The central rate is 7.46038 crowns to the euro.\par \par \uc2 * The normal trading band in the ERM II around the central parity is +/-15 percent. The \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, has set a narrower corridor of plus or minus 2.25 percent on either side of the central parity. The crown has historically been stable around the central parity rate at +/-0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 * Because it is pegged so closely to the euro exchange rate, and \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rates are the same as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's, the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is effectively the same as the euro, although the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no say in ECB's monetary policy decisions.\par \par \uc2 * Should markets push the exchange rate of the Danish crown outside the agreed band, the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would coordinate \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to keep the crown within the set corridor.\par \par \uc2 * The ECB and the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can agree to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market while the crown is still well within the band.\par \par \uc2 * When the crown is about to breach the band limits, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is automatic and unlimited. The only limiting factor would be if the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might threaten the overriding objective of price stability.\par \par \uc2 * The Danish government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  together with euro zone finance ministers and the ECB can agree to change the central parity rate and the process can be confidential until it is agreed.\par \par \uc2 * Denmark, like Britain, has a formal opt-out from joining the euro, so it has no formal obligation to be in the ERM II.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Jan Strupczewski; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-23T14:08:27.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150120eb1k00fcu\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Denmark  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Cuts Key Rates\b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2015\par \uc2 RTT News\par \uc2 RTTNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2015 NoticiasFinancieras. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (RTTNews) - Denmark cut its key interest rate unexpectedly on Monday ahead of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy meeting on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Nationalbank's lending rate and interest rate on certificates of deposit were reduced by 0.15 percentage point each. The lending rate was lowered to 0.05 percent from 0.2 percent and the deposit rate to -0.2 percent from -0.05 percent.\par \par \uc2 The discount rate and the current account rate are unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action came after the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  discontinued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceiling of Swiss franc and lowered its interest rate to -0.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 The move from the Denmark \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows steady upward pressure on the krone and could heighten speculation that the Nationalbank will ultimately have to abandon its peg to the euro, \uc2 Jessica Hinds\uc2 , a European economist at Capital Economics said.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come under more upward pressure once ECB quantitative easing is implemented and perhaps amid safe haven flows as an alternative to Switzerland, the economist noted.\par \par \uc2 The economist suspects that a further rate cut and additional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are to come in \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For comments and feedback: contact editorial@rttnews.com\par \par \uc2 Copyright(c) 2015 RTTNews.com. All Rights Reserved\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTTNEW0020150120eb1k0015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
