\par\par \b \uc2 Danish crown rises versus euro after Denmark rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2013\par 16:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 24 (Reuters) - The Danish crown rose to a session high against the euro on Thursday after \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates to stem recent falls and keep it within its trading band.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell to a low of 7.4612 crowns from around 7.4619 beforehand. It had dropped earlier in the day, with traders reporting talk of a rate hike.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the rate rise followed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to steady the crown.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of keeping its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading 2.25 percentage points around a central rate of 7.46038 against the euro. This means the crown can in theory fluctuate between 7.29252 and 7.62824, though in practice the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains a much tighter band.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jessica Mortimer)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /DANISH CROWN(URGENT) | ABN | D | M | DA | FN | NW | SW | RBN | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130124e91o000wj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
