\par\par \b \uc2 DJ \uc2 Danish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Seen Stepping Up Krone Defenses\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2012\par 15:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to change tact and support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --Krone weakness seen prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --Interest rates could be raised if krone weakness persists\par \par \uc2 By Clare Connaghan\par \par \uc2 The tide is turning in \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to weaken the krone. It is expected to make another foray soon -- this time to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Nationalbanken may even go so far as to raise interest rates to protect its precious peg, market participants say.\par \par \uc2 The bank's stated aim is to keep the krone trading within 2.25% either side of DKK7.46038 against the euro. In practice, the range has been much tighter, economists say.\par \par \uc2 "We are definitely now in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  zone, with the krone trading at levels where we expect the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in and start buying the krone to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Arne Lohmann Rasmussen, chief analyst at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  in Copenhagen.\par \par \uc2 The krone has weakened in recent months as tensions in the euro-zone ease, reducing investor appetite for safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the krone and Swiss franc. This after the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its deposit rate to minus 0.2%.\par \par \uc2 Having slipped below DKK7.43 as recently as June, the euro this week rose to its highest level against the krone in more than four years. At 1320 GMT, it was trading at DKK7.4590.\par \par \uc2 September data published last week shows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already begun to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a limited degree, after snapping up 600 million Danish kroner ($103.9 million).\par \par \uc2 But stronger action may be needed if the krone selloff picks up pace, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "The first line of defense will be for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  further to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jakob Lage Hansen, an investment strategist at \uc2 Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken\uc2 , also in Copenhagen.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may even have to raise interest rates, he added.\par \par \uc2 "If \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness persists, then the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would use interest rates as a second line of defense but we're not quite there yet," Mr. Hansen said.\par \par \uc2 Nationalbanken on July 5 cut its deposit rate to minus 0.2% from 0.05% and its policy lending rate to 0.2% from 0.45%. That was the same day the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the interest rate on its deposit facility to zero and its main policy rate to 0.75%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Clare Connaghan at clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 12, 2012 09:54 ET (13:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121012e8ac003d8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
