\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Danish cbank net crown buyer, 1st time in 18 months\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2012\par 16:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to 513.5 bln DKK in Sept\par \par \uc2 * Nationalbank says bought net 0.6 bln Danish crowns\par \par \uc2 * Analysts see rate hike later this year\par \par \uc2 (Adds context, analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Oct 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in September, becoming a net buyer of the Danish crown for the first time since March 2011.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a monetary policy tool, fell by 0.9 billion crowns in the month to 513.5 billion Danish crowns ($88.9 billion), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It bought a net 0.6 billion Danish crowns for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steady the crown in line with its mandate. Since March 2011, it had been either a net seller of the crown or not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at all.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a European Union member but euro zone outsider, had been attracting investor interest as a safe haven from the euro sovereign debt crisis. But the upward pressure on the crown has eased with renewed EU efforts to contain the crisis.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seeking to prevent a further weakening of the crown as investors' appetite for risk revived somewhat during September.\par \par \uc2 "With the support purchase in September, Denmark's Nationalbank has taken its first step towards the first independent Danish interest rate increase since the end of 2008," Nordea analyst Jan Stoerup Nielsen wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on a rather small scale and that the total net purchase would have to be closer to 15 billion crowns before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took any action on rates.\par \par \uc2 He added, however, that a rate hike could come within the next three months.\par \par \uc2 Sydbank also said the net purchase was so modest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely keep interest rates unchanged.\par \par \uc2 "If the crown weakens further, Denmark's Nationalbank will undoubtedly buy again, and then a hike becomes a reality," Sydbank chief economist Jacob Graven said.\par \par \uc2 Such actions by the bank tend to precede changes in interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Denmark's policy of holding the crown steady against the euro means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts interest rates for the sole purpose of keeping the crown around its central parity of 7.46038 per euro. ($1 = 5.7773 Danish crowns)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Mia Shanley and Teis Jensen; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 DENMARK-RESERVES/  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | DA | FN | NW | SW | RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121002e8a2000q3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
