\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Danish  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves slip, no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in April\b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2012\par 16:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes, background, crown rate)\par \par \uc2 * Reserves fall to 482.0 bln DKK in April\par \par \uc2 * C.bank says it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, May 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a monetary policy tool, fell slightly in April, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to steady the crown during the month.\par \par \uc2 The crown has been strong for months as investors wary of the European debt crisis have diversified out of euro assets and piled into non-euro holdings, including Danish government and mortgage bonds.\par \par \uc2 The Nationalbank, which runs a fixed exchange-rate monetary policy to keep the crown steady within a narrow band to the euro, can use the reserves to defend the peg, buying or selling crowns to bolster or weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The reserves fell by 1.1 billion crowns in April to 482.0 billion Danish crowns ($85.70 billion), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The drop stemmed from the bank's net sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for 0.4 billion crowns and the government's repayment of foreign debt for 0.6 billion, it said.\par \par \uc2 The median forecast in a Reuters survey of analysts had been for a rise to 484.5 billion crowns.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in April to steady the crown.\par \par \uc2 The reserves fell for a second consecutive month after a steep drop in March and remain below a peak of 498.7 billion crowns set in February.\par \par \uc2 "There are many signs that capital inflows from abroad have diminished in strength, so the Nationalbank did not find it necessary to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold the crown steady to the euro," Nykredit Markets senior economist Tore Stramer said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 Stramer said he still saw a chance that the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make an independent rate cut of 10 basis points in the coming months, but he noted that the crown had softened a bit and spreads to Germany narrowed recently.\par \par \uc2 "If this tendency continues in the coming weeks, the Nationalbank will, in our view, refrain from a further independent rate reduction," Stramer said.\par \par \uc2 The Nationalbank usually changes rates in lock-step with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rate spread to the euro zone steady, but the Danish bank can also alter rates independently to curb or support the crown within its band.\par \par \uc2 Changes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are a pointer to interest rate setting if they stem from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market because such action by the bank tends to precede changes in interest rates.\par \par \uc2 European Union member but euro outsider Denmark's policy of holding the crown steady against the euro means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts interest rates for the sole purpose of keeping the crown around its central parity of 7.46038 per euro.\par \par \uc2 Under the ERM II system, the crown is permitted to fluctuate by plus or minus 2.25 percent around that parity, and therefore between 7.29252 and 7.62824 per euro, though in practice the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps an even tighter range.\par \par \uc2 The crown was at 7.4384 to the euro by 1425 GMT, unchanged from levels just before the bank's announcement. ($1 = 5.6246 Danish crowns)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by John Acher; Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 DENMARK-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | DA | FN | NW | SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120502e852000zt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
