\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Danish  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves record high, no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2012\par 16:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Reserves rise to 492.6 bln DKK in Jan\par \par \uc2 * End-2012 reserves adjusted up by 10.2 bln DKK\par \par \uc2 * C.bank did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steady the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Feb 2 (Reuters) - Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves climbed to a new all-time high in January after their end-2011 level was adjusted upwards, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  having refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steady the crown last month.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2  runs a fixed exchange-rate monetary policy, and the level of reserves is a pointer to policy as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can use them to regulate the value of the crown. The bank said on Thursday it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in January.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by 0.7 billion crowns in January to 492.6 billion crowns ($87.46 billion), the Nationalbank said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 That small increase followed an upward adjustment of the end-December value of the reserves by 10.2 billion crowns to a then-record 491.9 billion crowns, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 The revised December level exceeded a previous peak of 490.3 billion crowns set in September last year.\par \par \uc2 The bank said the rise in reserves in January reflected its net purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , equivalent to 1.2 billion crowns, and net repayment by the central government of 0.4 billion crowns' worth of foreign debt.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like the massive pressure on the crown that has been there for some time is diminishing," Nykredit senior economist Tore Stramer said. "The crown has been stable against the euro through January."\par \par \uc2 European Union member Denmark's policy of holding the crown steady against the euro means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts interest rates for the sole purpose of keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around its central parity of 7.46038 per euro.\par \par \uc2 The crown was strong throughout 2011 and has remained strong in early 2012 as foreign investors snap up Danish assets in a bid to diversify away from the crisis-hit euro zone.\par \par \uc2 "The huge foreign reserve is above all a reflection of the fact that investors have great faith in the Danish economy," Sydbank chief economist Jacob Graven said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in December to curb the Danish unit's strength., selling a net 17.8 billion crowns for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It also cut its main policy rate, the lending rate, twice in December, by a total of 0.5 percentage points, putting Danish rates 30 basis points below the main European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, and many analysts say the Nationalbank is likely to cut further.\par \par \uc2 STEADY CROWN\par \par \uc2 Nordea senior analyst Jan Storup Nielsen noted that the crown stayed in a very tight range of 7.433-7.436 in January without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Over the coming months, we believe that the Nationalbank will try to keep EUR/DKK around the same level," he said.\par \par \uc2 The crown firmed slightly, to 7.4330 to the euro by 1712 GMT from 7.4333 just before the bank's announcement.\par \par \uc2 If appetite for Danish crowns is sustained, the Nationalbank may be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would add billions more to the already hefty reserves, said Nielsen.\par \par \uc2 "Still, we see a high likelihood that over the next three months it will be necessary to carry out another independent Danish rate cut to offset the continuing (strengthening) pressure on the crown," he added.\par \par \uc2 Nykredit's Stramer said the spread between Danish and German 10-year government bond yields has been close to nil after dipping earlier into negative territory, indicating that foreign investors' appetite for Danish assets has declined.\par \par \uc2 "This does not mean, however, that international investors are looking at the Danish economy more critically," Stramer said. "They are just beginning to believe that the politicians will reach a more sustainable solution to the debt crisis in the euro area and that the euro will not collapse." ($1 = 5.6324 Danish crowns)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by John Acher and Henriette Jacobsen; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 DENMARK-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120205e822000h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
