\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Danish  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves dip, no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in Oct\b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2011\par 16:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Nov 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell slightly in October, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw no reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to steady the crown during the month, the bank said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by the equivalent of 400 million crowns in October to 489.9 billion Danish crowns ($90.04 billion), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 It was the first dip in the reserves since May, so the reserves -- a pointer to monetary policy -- remain near record high levels.\par \par \uc2 "The Nationalbank was not out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the month even though we saw a considerable strengthening of the crown towards the end of the month to levels where it is not unusual for the bank to sell crowns and buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown," Nordea Markets senior analyst Troels Theill Eriksen said.\par \par \uc2 If such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fails to have the desired effect, the bank changes interest rates to weaken or strengthen the crown within its band to the euro.\par \par \uc2 The crown remains strong and short Danish money market interest rates are somewhat higher than corresponding rates in the euro zone, which also tends to boost the crown.\par \par \uc2 "Therefore there are prospects for the Nationalbank before long to choose to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown and follow up with an independent interest rate rise if the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not lead to a durable weakening of the crown," Eriksen said.\par \par \uc2 European Union member but euro zone outsider Denmark's policy of holding the crown steady against the euro means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts interest rates for the sole purpose of keeping the crown around its central parity of 7.46038 per euro\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Danish bank normally changes rates in lock-step with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is not expected to change rates at its meeting on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Danish bank can, however, opt to make independent rate changes above all in its secondary interest rates to boost or curb the crown.\par \par \uc2 Eriksen said he expected the Nationalbank to cut its certificates of deposit (CD) rate soon to 0.9 percent from 1.0 percent and ECB to cut interest rates by 0.5 percentage point over the next six months, which the Danish bank would shadow with cuts in its lending rate which now stands at 1.55 percent.\par \par \uc2 The decrease in the October reserves reflected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for 0.4 billion crowns and the central government's net foreign borrowing of 0.1 billion, the Nationalbank said. ($1 = 5.441 Danish crowns)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Copenhagen newsroom)\par \par \uc2 DENMARK-RESERVES/  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111105e7b2000ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
