\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Danish  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves hit new peak, rate rise looms\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2011\par 16:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Reserves rise to record-high 453.9 bln DKK at end-March\par \par \uc2 * C.bank says \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for 0.4 bln DKK\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen hiking rates this week, shadowing ECB\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, April 4 (Reuters) - Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by 7.4 billion Danish crowns in March to a new all-time high of 453.9 billion, despite a small \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are watched as pointer to the Danish monetary policy, but they are wholly eclipsed in importance this week by an expected rate rise the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which analysts said would trigger a similar move by the Nationalbank.\par \par \uc2 Denmark's reserves rose for a third consecutive month, climbing from February's record level of 446.4 billion, though analysts had expected a small drop in March.\par \par \uc2 The Nationalbank, which runs a fixed exchange-rate monetary policy to keep the crown within a narrow band to the euro, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in March by selling a net 0.4 billion crowns worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for crowns, it said.\par \par \uc2 "The crown weakened in the first half of March, which led the Nationalbank to make support purchases to strengthen the crown," Nordea Markets senior analyst Troels Theill Eriksen said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in January and February after only a small \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December.\par \par \uc2 European Union member but euro zone outsider \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of holding the crown steady against the euro means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts interest rates for the sole purpose of keeping the crown around its central parity of 7.46038 per euro <EURDKK=>.\par \par \uc2 DENMARK TO FOLLOW ECB\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to raise interest rates on Thursday for the first time since October 2008, and economists said the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was certain to follow on the same day with the same-sized rate increase.\par \par \uc2 "It is given that they would follow with 25 basis points which is what we expect the ECB to do," Eriksen told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Seventy-six out of 80 analysts polled by last week said they expected the ECB to raise its policy rate by 25 bps from a record low 1.0 percent as the bank focuses on curbing inflation. [ID:nSLAUEE7RO]\par \par \uc2 "On Thursday, you will see the ECB raising rates and then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  here raising at 4 p.m. (1400 GMT)," \uc2 Jyske Bank\uc2  economist Niels Ronholt told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 If the ECB raises rates this week, the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would follow by raising all its official rates, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "On Thursday they would take them all up," Ronholt said.\par \par \uc2 It would be the first increase in the bank's main policy rate, the lending rate, since October 2008 when Denmark raised by 50 basis points to a peak of 5.50 percent to defend the crown just as the world slid into financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The lending rate has been steady at an all-time low 1.05 percent since January 2010. A rise to 1.30 percent would put it back to levels it last saw in August-September 2009 when the bank was cutting rates.\par \par \uc2 The Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began tightening independently in October 2010, however, with two 10 bps increases in a secondary rate, its certificates of deposit rate.\par \par \uc2 If the bank changes rates on Thursday, it would lift the lending rate, CD rate and current account rate, economists said.\par \par \uc2 "We expect them to make the same hike on all the rates...this time around because the crown is fairly strong and the interest rate spreads are sound now so there is no reason for them to do anything independently," Eriksen said\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 DENMARK-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110407e7440010m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
