\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Danish  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves fall, no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  -c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2010\par 16:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves retreat from record high\par \par \uc2 * C.bank says it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in April\par \par \uc2 * April \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fall by 13.1 bln\par \par \uc2 * Analysts don't rule out another rate cut\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes, crown rate)\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, May 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to steady the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, and the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell for the first time since October.\par \par \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to 404.1 billion Danish crowns ($72.3 billion) from a record level of 417.2 billion in March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The Nationalbank said its net purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  were 0.3 billion, but the government's net repayment of debt amounted to 13.4 billion, leading to the overall net drop in the reserves.\par \par \uc2 Changes in the foreign reserves can signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stabilising the crown or suggest that the bank is preparing to change its key interest rates. The bank nonetheless left interest rates unchanged on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "The interesting thing is that they did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the crown being at a relatively strong level," Handelsbanken Capital Markets chief economist Jes Asmussen said.\par \par \uc2 "The conclusion is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't seem worried about the level of the crown. This diminshes expectations of another rate cut," Asmussen added.\par \par \uc2 "Our main forecast is that the lending rate has reached bottom at 1.05 percent, although there is still a risk that there will be another cut. The rate will only start coming up again once the euro zone money market has normalised," he said.\par \par \uc2 European Union member but euro zone outsider Denmark's policy of holding the crown steady against the euro means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts interest rates for the sole purpose of keeping the crown within a narrow band around its central parity of 7.46038 per euro <EURDKK=>.\par \par \uc2 Persistent inflows into the crown -- the reserves are up from 286.4 billion crowns in April last year and a many-year low of 161.9 billion in May 2008 -- have kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strong for months and forced the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the market to curb its strength.\par \par \uc2 The crown softened briefly to 7.4431 the euro <EURDKK=> from 7.4426 just before the announcement, but returned to 7.4427 by 1430 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Crown strength has compelled the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates 14 times from a peak of 5.50 percent in late 2008 to an all-time low of 1.05 percent. Its latest cut, 10 basis points, came in January.\par \par \uc2 Danske Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst John Hydeskov said there was a chance of another 10 basis points cut in the bank's certificate of deposit rate -- a secondary rate which now lies at 0.70 percent -- within the next weeks.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by John Acher and Anna Ringstrom)\par \par \uc2 DENMARK-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100507e654001nb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
