\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Danish Oct  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves fall to 376.1 bln DKK\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2009\par 16:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fall, against expectation of no change\par \par \uc2 * Economists say rate cuts have worked to dampen inflows\par \par \uc2 * Economists say drop in reserves eases rate cut pressure\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Nov 3 (Reuters) - Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by 17.8 billion crowns to 376.1 billion Danish crowns ($73.96 billion) in October against economists' expectation of no change, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Analysts surveyed by Reuters had estimated that the reserves remained unchanged in October at the September level of 393.8 billion crowns, according to the median of five forecasts.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the drop in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves -- the first decrease in the monthly figure since October 2008 -- indicated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate cuts have curbed inflows into the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had sold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the month for a net 0.1 billion crowns and the central government repaid foreign loans worth 17.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 Changes in the foreign reserves can signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stabilising the crown or indicate that the bank may change its key interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "In October, \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Nationalbank has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 European Union member but euro zone outsider Denmark's policy of holding the crown steady against the euro means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts interest rates for the sole purpose of keeping the crown around its central parity of 7.46038 per euro <EURDKK=>.\par \par \uc2 Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves climbed steeply from the late 2008 until September this year as interest rate spreads between Denmark and the euro zone initially widened in the financial and economic crisis, making crown investments attractive.\par \par \uc2 But the spread to the euro zone has narrowed, with Denmark's policy rate now just a quarter point above the euro zone's 1 percent after 10 Danish rate cuts lopped 4.25 percentage points off the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lending rate since November 2008.\par \par \uc2 Market interest rate spreads remain wider than the gap between official rates, but have also narrowed.\par \par \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  economist Tore Stramer said in a note to clients that the Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independent rate cuts since June succeeded in dampening the inflows of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and thereby curbed pressures on the crown.\par \par \uc2 "Looking ahead, we expect to see a further narrowing of the rate spread, which will to a significant degree contribute to dampening inflows of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pressure on the crown," Stramer said.\par \par \uc2 "Much seems to indicate that the little opening we had seen for yet another small rate reduction of 0.10 percent from the Nationalbank before the turn of the year is now finally about to be closed," he added.\par \par \uc2 Stramer said he did not expect a further Danish rate cut until the big rollover of Danish mortgage bonds in November-December.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 DENMARK-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|DA|FN|NW|SW|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091103e5b3001p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
