\par\par \b \uc2 Danish Ctrl Bk Raises Key Lending Rate To 4.35% From 4.25%\b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2008\par 10:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM (Dow Jones)--The Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked its key rate Friday in a move defending the pegged Danish krone exchange rate against the euro, as it made its first unilateral action on rates since February 2006.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its lending rate and the interest rate for certificates of deposits to 4.35% from 4.25%.\par \par \uc2 "Since August 2007 the spread between Danmarks Nationalbank's lending rate and the ECB's marginal rate has been reduced by 15 basis points to 20 basis points, thus the spread has more or less disappeared. In short periods of time the interest-rate spread has been negative," the bank said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "Due to the increased spread, there has been a weakening of the Danish krone, and in accordance with the fixed-exchange-rate policy Danmarks Nationalbank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the krone," the bank added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged to the euro, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has routinely kept its key rate at 25 basis points above the ECB's key rate in order to defend the fixed exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 When the ECB moves rates, Denmark usually follows suit with an equivalent move later the same day.\par \par \uc2 The last time Danmarks Nationalbank made a unilateral rate move was in February 2006, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Bank Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.nationalbanken.dk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.nationalbanken.dk}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Joel Sherwood, Dow Jones Newswires, +46 85 45 13 092, joel.sherwood@dowjones.com [ 16-05-08 0855GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080516e45g000ht\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
