\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Danish c.bank raises interest rates to help crown\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2008\par 10:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  quote)\par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN, May 16 (Reuters) - Denmark's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key one-week interest rate by 10 basis points on Friday, saying it acted to counter a weakening of the Danish crown. \par \par \uc2  The bank said it raised its one-week certificates of deposits and lending rates to 4.35 percent from 4.25 percent. The less important discount rate remained unchanged at 4.0 percent.\par \par \uc2  "The development in the interest rate spread has led to a weakening of the Danish crown, so in accordance with the fixed exchange rate policy the national bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown," the Danish bank said.  \par \par \uc2  Although \b \highlight22\uc2 Denmark\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a European Union member, has not adopted the euro, it has a long-standing policy of keeping the crown stable against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  This means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts key interest rates for the sole purpose of keeping the crown around its central parity of 7.46038 per euro <EURDKK=>.\par \par \uc2  Usually the national bank changes its rates the same day and by the same margin as the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has kept rates at 4 percent since last June. The last time the Danish bank acted on its own was February 2006.\par \par \uc2  The bank said that the spread between the Danish bank's lending rate and the rate at which the ECB lends to banks at its money market tenders has been shrinking since August 2007 and lately had sometimes become negative.\par \par \uc2  "The rate increase has strengthened the crown, but not a lot," said Jes Asmussen, chief economist at Handelsbanken. "It was on the cards, but timing is of course always a surprise."\par \par \uc2   The crown, which strengthened as far as 7.45 to the euro in early March, weakened to 7.4636 on Friday before bouncing back to 7.4594 after the rate hike.\par \par \uc2  (Reporting by Gelu Sulugiuc; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)  \par \par \uc2 DENMARK-C.BANK/RATES (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|DA|FN|NW|SW|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080516e45g001kf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
